# Learning and Building AI Agents from Scratch

## 1. Fundamentals
- Understand what Artificial Intelligence (AI) is.
- Learn what an "agent" means in AI—perception, reasoning, and action.
- Types of agents: reflex, model-based, goal-based, utility-based.

**Resources:**
- [AIMA Book (Russell & Norvig)](https://aima.cs.berkeley.edu/)
- [Stanford CS221 Lectures](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLoROMvodv4rO1NB9TD4iUZ3qghGEGtqNX)

---

## 2. Python Programming Basics
- Learn Python syntax, functions, classes, and data structures.

**Resources:**
- [Official Python Tutorial](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/)

---

## 3. Build a Simple Reflex Agent

### Example Project: Reflex Agent in a Grid World

Steps:
1. Define the environment (e.g., simple 5x5 grid).
2. Define agent perception (its position, whether there’s a wall).
3. Define agent actions (move up, down, left, right).
4. Implement simple rules (e.g., always move right if possible, else move down).

---

## 4. Search & Planning
- Learn about state spaces, actions, transition models.
- Study search algorithms: Breadth-First Search (BFS), Depth-First Search (DFS), A*.

---

## 5. Machine Learning (ML) & Reinforcement Learning (RL)
- Understand basics of supervised, unsupervised, and RL.
- Learn about Q-learning and value-based methods.

**Resources:**
- [OpenAI Gym](https://gym.openai.com/)
- [David Silver’s RL Course](https://www.davidsilver.uk/teaching/)

---

## 6. Build a Learning Agent
- Implement a Q-learning agent in a grid world.
- Experiment with different environments and rewards.

---

## 7. Expand & Experiment
- Try building: simple chatbots, game AI, or multi-agent systems.
- Contribute to open source, join AI communities, and participate in competitions (Kaggle, AIcrowd).

